{
  "tema": 5121,
  "slug": "lo-la-los-las-objeto-directo",
  "titulo": "Direct object pronouns lo, la, los, las",
  "subtitulo": "¿El taco? Ya lo comí.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "Lo, la, los, las replace a direct object (him, her, it, them, formal you) and match its gender and number. They go before a conjugated verb, or can attach to the end of an infinitive or gerund.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **direct object** receives the action: **compro el pan**. To avoid repeating it, replace it with **lo, la, los, las**: **lo compro**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Pronoun",
            "Replaces",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "**lo**",
              "him, it (masc.), you (usted, masc.)",
              "**Lo** veo."
            ],
            [
              "**la**",
              "her, it (fem.), you (usted, fem.)",
              "**La** veo."
            ],
            [
              "**los**",
              "them (masc. or mixed), you all (masc. or mixed)",
              "**Los** veo."
            ],
            [
              "**las**",
              "them (fem.), you all (fem.)",
              "**Las** veo."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Match the **noun**, not the English: **la tabla** → **la**, **los tacos** → **los**. A mixed group takes **los**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Position: **before** the conjugated verb. With **no**, **no** comes first."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "(no)",
            "+ lo / la / los / las +",
            "conjugated verb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With an infinitive or gerund, you can also attach it: **lo voy a comprar** = **voy a comprarlo**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Subject _it_ is never said in Spanish: _it is expensive_ = **es caro**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿El taco? Ya ==lo== comí.",
              "en": "The taco? I already ate it."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Conoces a Marta? Sí, ==la== conozco del gimnasio.",
              "en": "Do you know Marta? Yes, I know her from the gym."
            },
            {
              "es": "Compré tortillas y ==las== puse en la mesa.",
              "en": "I bought tortillas and put them on the table."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Dónde están los guantes? No ==los== encuentro.",
              "en": "Where are the gloves? I can't find them."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ves a Juan y a Lupe? Sí, ==los== veo.",
              "en": "Do you see Juan and Lupe? Yes, I see them."
            },
            {
              "es": "Las plantas tienen sed. ¿==Las== puedes regar?",
              "en": "The plants are thirsty. Can you water them?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Señor, ¿==lo== ayudo con las bolsas?",
              "en": "Sir, can I help you with the bags?"
            },
            {
              "es": "La tabla está rota, pero ==la== voy a arreglar mañana.",
              "en": "The board is broken, but I'm going to fix it tomorrow."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
